cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [303, 1293, 1465, 1409, 28],\n  \"window\": [37896, 57095],\n  \"confidence\": 0.57,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"303 emits only two events (to 1409 and 1465); neither successor reaches 1293 within two hops. Any static route must pass through hub 28 (150 in-neighbours), which explains time-ignoring connectivity but is not a targeted chain. Temporally, 303's later event (~53.1k) postdates 1293's final event (~52.8k), and the earlier 303 event would require a 4-hop, \u2264600-per-hop relay through the hub for which no supporting activity pattern was observed. Conclusion: no genuine time-respecting cascade from 303 to 1293 in this window.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 27905, "total_output_tokens": 7283, "total_tokens": 35188, "total_latency_ms": 95917, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}